blindsight 0.1.0: offline verification of a Safe transaction (verify)

CRITICAL: DO NOT SIGN without independent review
Findings: 2 critical, 1 low, 1 info
A clean result does not make a transaction safe: blindsight does not simulate it. Compare the hashes below with your wallet.

FINDINGS (4)
  CRITICAL  BS-DELEGATE-001   root
            Delegatecall to a contract that is not an official Safe helper
            This call runs the code at
            0x96221423681A6d52E184D440a8eFCEbB105C7242 with the storage of
            0x1Db92e2EeBC8E0c075a02BeA49a2935BcD2dFCF4 (this Safe). That code
            can replace the owners, threshold, modules, guard, fallback handler
            and the implementation pointer in storage slot 0, after which the
            attacker no longer needs any signature. This is how the Bybit (2025)
            and WazirX (2024) Safes were taken over. Do not sign unless you have
            reviewed the target's source and know why it needs delegatecall.
  CRITICAL  BS-SEMANTICS-001  root
            "transfer" is a guess from the selector, not a verified function
            The calldata matches transfer(address,uint256), but
            0x96221423681A6d52E184D440a8eFCEbB105C7242 is not known to implement
            it: under delegatecall a token function moves no tokens: the
            target's code runs on the Safe's own storage. Any contract can give
            a function this signature and do something else; the Bybit attack
            used transfer(address,uint256), executed by delegatecall, to replace
            the Safe's implementation. Treat the decoded name and arguments as a
            layout, not as a description.
  LOW       BS-REPLAY-001     root
            Signature valid on every chain
            Safe 1.1.1 has no chain id in its signing domain, so this signature
            is also valid on any other chain where a Safe exists at
            0x1Db92e2EeBC8E0c075a02BeA49a2935BcD2dFCF4 with the same nonce. Make
            sure no such Safe exists, or that it is under the same control.
  INFO      BS-TARGET-001     root
            Unknown target
            0x96221423681A6d52E184D440a8eFCEbB105C7242 is not an official Safe
            contract, a listed token or an address-book entry. Check it against
            a source you trust (add it to your address book to label it).

